{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"e649ef40336508b50cf38eb24e3e5e91dad83dc1e8f44d4707f1df7a9bbfbc80","slug":"blog.2018.my-workflow","location":"/blog/2018/my-workflow.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"My weekly workflow","tags":["productivity"],"date":"2018-10-26","content_includes_title":false,"authors":[{"id":"chris","nameParsed":{"literal":"Chris Holdgraf","given":"Chris","family":"Holdgraf"},"name":"Chris Holdgraf","orcid":"0000-0002-2391-0678","affiliations":["affiliations-myst-generated-uid-0","affiliations-myst-generated-uid-1"],"url":"https://chrisholdgraf.com","github":"choldgraf","twitter":"choldgraf"}],"github":"https://github.com/choldgraf/choldgraf.github.io","affiliations":[{"name":"2i2c","url":"https://2i2c.org","id":"affiliations-myst-generated-uid-0"},{"name":"Project Jupyter","url":"https://jupyter.org","id":"affiliations-myst-generated-uid-1"}],"abbreviations":{"LF":"The Linux Foundation","JF":"The Jupyter Foundation","JEC":"Jupyter Executive Council","JFB":"The Jupyter Foundation Board","SSC":"Software Steering Council","OSPO":"Open Source Program Office"},"numbering":{"title":{"offset":2}},"source_url":"https://github.com/choldgraf/choldgraf.github.io/blob/main/blog/2018/my-workflow.md","edit_url":"https://github.com/choldgraf/choldgraf.github.io/edit/main/blog/2018/my-workflow.md","thumbnail":"/build/trello-board-project-f00048dca512b65d7f29973ae5df4e93.png","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"my-workflow.md","url":"/build/my-workflow-c12e73081fbbff55f8ae2494a94c8f96.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"I’ve had a bunch of conversations with friends who were interested in how to\nkeep track of the various projects they’re working on, and to prioritize their\ntime over the course of a week. I thought it might be helpful to post my own\napproach to planning time throughout the week in case it’s useful for others to\nriff off of.","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"key":"BYQFEXNM5w"}],"key":"sMcN0tAldo"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"General principles","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"key":"RPqTEVTX8q"}],"identifier":"general-principles","label":"General principles","html_id":"general-principles","implicit":true,"key":"ZliowB3RWz"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"First off, a few general principles that I use to guide my thinking on planning\nout the week.","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"key":"obLXhc88JU"}],"key":"S1wDHLjp8k"},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Be intentional.","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"key":"hqb0o0qPdK"}],"key":"ogthgoQNuA"},{"type":"text","value":" This seems obvious, but I find that if I don’t explicitly define\nwhat I want to work on, I have more of those “where the heck did the day go” kinds\nof weeks.","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"key":"cxFAdFHg9I"}],"key":"RkhTMhisyq"}],"key":"Sg5bKeHAve"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":25,"column":1},"end":{"line":27,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":25,"column":1},"end":{"line":25,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Be strategic.","position":{"start":{"line":25,"column":1},"end":{"line":25,"column":1}},"key":"CWeynLLtxJ"}],"key":"Wd8tGVp8QY"},{"type":"text","value":" There are only so many hours in the day, which means that I need to be\ncareful about what I commit to spending time on. I try to figure out what are the most\nimportant things to do, and ensure I make space for this work before other stuff.","position":{"start":{"line":25,"column":1},"end":{"line":25,"column":1}},"key":"r6h9QfNur7"}],"key":"YJuikqi27d"}],"key":"ogok9vQusP"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":28,"column":1},"end":{"line":30,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":28,"column":1},"end":{"line":28,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Be (conservatively) realistic.","position":{"start":{"line":28,"column":1},"end":{"line":28,"column":1}},"key":"KnL5nYIloW"}],"key":"mChZiC60dB"},{"type":"text","value":" I often get too optimistic with my time and energy levels.\nSometimes you’re tired, sometimes you get distracted, sometimes new work pops up you didn’t\naccount for. For this reason, I only budget about ","position":{"start":{"line":28,"column":1},"end":{"line":28,"column":1}},"key":"ibYDtWq61C"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":28,"column":1},"end":{"line":28,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"20 hours of diligent work a week","position":{"start":{"line":28,"column":1},"end":{"line":28,"column":1}},"key":"AWUKkdHgwc"}],"key":"mdDs4D1vaO"},{"type":"text","value":".","position":{"start":{"line":28,"column":1},"end":{"line":28,"column":1}},"key":"kYmxohgXa9"}],"key":"Q4ivA3hPmW"}],"key":"eH1HbFyO65"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":32,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Be flexible.","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"key":"mKsArykMax"}],"key":"HrfcWJUNfo"},{"type":"text","value":" Finally, don’t worry about following the plan obsessively. Use it as a guide,\nnot a set of chains. If it’s worth re-prioritizing, that’s fine!","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"key":"kE0FAqzt6J"}],"key":"yDe6roQQ6c"}],"key":"V7VMPCsoXK"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Be diligent.","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"key":"qkqofrWUUb"}],"key":"x70uPcW2LO"},{"type":"text","value":" That said, whenever the plans ","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"key":"hcFCM90qqN"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"do","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"key":"g30MZVSR7h"}],"key":"Z8JHD0Jn4r"},{"type":"text","value":" change, make sure that this is written down\nsomewhere so that I know I’m being intentional about it.","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"key":"bUD47hZ7yo"}],"key":"QrbTkgrhde"}],"key":"YuGRxuRxzJ"}],"key":"qbUNC3bxh5"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":36,"column":1},"end":{"line":36,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"What tools do I use?","position":{"start":{"line":36,"column":1},"end":{"line":36,"column":1}},"key":"qYhHDSLaeQ"}],"identifier":"what-tools-do-i-use","label":"What tools do I use?","html_id":"what-tools-do-i-use","implicit":true,"key":"qTbfyZBc02"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"OK so what does this process actually look like? Here’s a general approach:","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"key":"AgQmO3OFF7"}],"key":"xCwasiZN8L"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"I use ","position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"column":1}},"key":"r3An6kYXWs"},{"type":"link","url":"https://trello.com/","position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Trello","position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"column":1}},"key":"g27D9fSQrL"}],"key":"LxnKL7MDYH"}],"urlSource":"https://trello.com/","key":"gQZumQwQca"},{"type":"text","value":" for managing most of the projects that I work on each week. For those who aren’t familiar,\nTrello is a web app that lets you organize “cards” into vertical lists. It’s useful for Kanban-style\nproject management, and is super popular in technical circles.","position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"column":1}},"key":"XabnsLM3Bk"}],"key":"Sd4vRUD4o7"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"I use two kinds of Trello boards, “project” boards, and my “weekly” board.","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"key":"XBYhg7W107"}],"key":"YgQfurHusj"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":46,"column":1},"end":{"line":46,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Project boards","position":{"start":{"line":46,"column":1},"end":{"line":46,"column":1}},"key":"fh1pWrF6hP"}],"identifier":"project-boards","label":"Project boards","html_id":"project-boards","implicit":true,"key":"chOIe2werI"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":48,"column":1},"end":{"line":48,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Project boards are project-specific. They’re organized in four primary columns.","position":{"start":{"line":48,"column":1},"end":{"line":48,"column":1}},"key":"HAYEalQaTI"}],"key":"APM68ML6jx"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":50,"column":1},"end":{"line":55,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":50,"column":1},"end":{"line":50,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":50,"column":1},"end":{"line":50,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Info","position":{"start":{"line":50,"column":1},"end":{"line":50,"column":1}},"key":"sOQEMzf6Nh"}],"key":"v8rhaNSg30"},{"type":"text","value":" has cards with information about that project. For example, links, notes, attachments, etc.","position":{"start":{"line":50,"column":1},"end":{"line":50,"column":1}},"key":"ZeKNYTwUAM"}],"key":"y247QMqc6R"}],"key":"OYfStW6SoQ"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":51,"column":1},"end":{"line":52,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":51,"column":1},"end":{"line":51,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"ToDo","position":{"start":{"line":51,"column":1},"end":{"line":51,"column":1}},"key":"h7A3iNZDEx"}],"key":"biEweL7tsR"},{"type":"text","value":" has cards representing tasks that I’ll do eventually. These tend to be more abstract and\nwill evolve over time.","position":{"start":{"line":51,"column":1},"end":{"line":51,"column":1}},"key":"w4nH65tDEr"}],"key":"ZrNt30x1wU"}],"key":"WypDzeXgj0"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":53,"column":1},"end":{"line":53,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":53,"column":1},"end":{"line":53,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next","position":{"start":{"line":53,"column":1},"end":{"line":53,"column":1}},"key":"HjLcdpTH5S"}],"key":"q1yqaXsQVE"},{"type":"text","value":" has cards representing actionable tasks that I’ll do soon.","position":{"start":{"line":53,"column":1},"end":{"line":53,"column":1}},"key":"n3btHptNPF"}],"key":"EwS9mfZT2D"}],"key":"yceAU6HhMH"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":54,"column":1},"end":{"line":55,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":54,"column":1},"end":{"line":54,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Doing","position":{"start":{"line":54,"column":1},"end":{"line":54,"column":1}},"key":"JFXFg4HpYA"}],"key":"THDIuV6qPu"},{"type":"text","value":" is a special list that I’ll explain later. It’s where cards go when I’m working on them currently.","position":{"start":{"line":54,"column":1},"end":{"line":54,"column":1}},"key":"uRRnKzVTEQ"}],"key":"Qn74oFuMUS"}],"key":"e8Wju9D9N8"}],"key":"YS9ODAVf9j"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":58,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The other major component of the projcet board is a collection of “Done” lists. At the end of each\nweek, and cards that are finished get moved into a list named like so: ","position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":56,"column":1}},"key":"hYnTMGl8vk"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":56,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Done - Week NN","position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":56,"column":1}},"key":"yypQV2AI8a"}],"key":"QD8TPApaQK"},{"type":"text","value":" where “NN” is the\nnumber of the current week.","position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":56,"column":1}},"key":"gtOOYsHBaY"}],"key":"f69r6C1F18"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":60,"column":1},"end":{"line":61,"column":1}},"chil